#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510449 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7d226d3-f7d3-574f-94f9-a532ec99b0ac" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Expression for a Least-Squares Solution in Terms of the Matrices Q and R"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aaeec0e-9d7d-51b5-8e98-ca8703231590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509775} {:answer/id #uuid "5a928cee-21d3-53ca-ace1-76f33e1c43e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Q" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509875} {:answer/id #uuid "ac5cc7e5-983e-54c2-88c3-dc3f7ef1cb76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510057} {:answer/id #uuid "b7edffd0-66a0-5c75-bcc7-1841cf561f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(Q-I)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510081} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c7732e-ce78-5352-8708-b204edd3100c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2aaeec0e-9d7d-51b5-8e98-ca8703231590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{Q}^{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509775} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cd33a2a-4f98-5342-9ba4-5873365eeaa6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c3b9fdd0-8dab-5a0b-9e88-9a8e531bca1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-139771" :question/problem "$$\nx={R}^{-1}\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\\,b\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}\\,\\,{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is ${Q}^{T}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510454 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133906 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c7d226d3-f7d3-574f-94f9-a532ec99b0ac" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Expression for a Least-Squares Solution in Terms of the Matrices Q and R"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2312d1c9-ae68-5003-ac7e-7414fd467ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509761} {:answer/id #uuid "425e926e-f6d7-5135-b061-818402d0d1d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509828} {:answer/id #uuid "73a71808-3fa5-573e-b8b1-b19de5e75149" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{b}^{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509931} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ae5c2d-37b1-5cab-9352-7357b57e7f85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{b}{‖b‖}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510048} {:answer/id #uuid "da0250e9-1d30-5606-9e21-317e8cba1e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{A}^{T}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2312d1c9-ae68-5003-ac7e-7414fd467ee9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509761} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4202d35-11cb-528d-8f7b-8baa57144892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510338}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb3d3dae-b723-59f7-8d1b-568e2e8664df" :question/math-academy-id "q-139772" :question/problem "$$\nx={R}^{-1}{Q}^{T}\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{A}}\n$$\n\nLet $A=QR$  be a QR decomposition of an $m\\times n$ matrix $A$ with linearly independent columns, and the expression above gives the least-squares solution of $Ax=b.$ What is the missing part of the equation?" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the normal equation\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nThen, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $R$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by ${R}^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{-1}\\cdot Rx & ={R}^{-1}\\cdot {Q}^{T}b \\\\ x & ={R}^{-1}{Q}^{T}\\,\\,b\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing part of the equation is $b.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510364 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d177b305-cdd1-5f91-b9d5-90623e52ad10" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System Given a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d72c52-be81-5a78-89ce-5f13fcd20525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509726} {:answer/id #uuid "39ecad14-1c0a-5aad-bfee-718224c4fd70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509813} {:answer/id #uuid "782b8fc8-baa5-5617-a0d8-b51e87778593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509943} {:answer/id #uuid "7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509956} {:answer/id #uuid "d0ba3a48-87bd-5410-a677-49fe3a6248f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ccbb9de-1d05-5669-a825-c1565d374612" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509956} :answer-field/id #uuid "551c0677-6855-511f-8997-47d81f6ef2d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02febb14-e263-5cc1-8053-2e425b9d6cc5" :question/math-academy-id "q-139783" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ is orthogonal, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-11 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}=-11 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-4(5) & =-11 \\\\ 3{x}_{1} & =9 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d177b305-cdd1-5f91-b9d5-90623e52ad10" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System Given a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cfa9745-27c9-5c69-9259-9f33cdd30cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410781} {:answer/id #uuid "290a80b2-d833-5e18-ba11-922da75fadbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410784} {:answer/id #uuid "84becdeb-7cb6-51f9-8247-37058f839cfa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410791} {:answer/id #uuid "ab331c8e-8ec8-5a70-b8c2-e3efcd32bf48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410795} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a2f5a3-da1b-5892-8fa1-25b99c4d869f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab331c8e-8ec8-5a70-b8c2-e3efcd32bf48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410795} :answer-field/id #uuid "44672c62-c008-5400-a940-292eccf518a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8892a71-2970-5d65-891c-76f1124825ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-139796" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{2} & -4\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}x & =\\begin{bmatrix}38\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}-4\\sqrt{2}{x}_{2}=38\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}=-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-5.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1}-4\\sqrt{2}(-5) & =38\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2}{x}_{1} & =18\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133803 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d177b305-cdd1-5f91-b9d5-90623e52ad10" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System Given a QR Factorization"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a1a00c1-8450-5a4b-9a89-eeb5fc22d5e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509711} {:answer/id #uuid "3c4ffb51-6024-5d55-874c-2de6b98d1d70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509818} {:answer/id #uuid "4c400c42-935c-5527-acc8-5171e1a58778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-10 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509845} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d240b2-f0ec-5826-be4a-8f21e8f0a799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510043} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f82732-0e5a-5d26-9566-a09f36539763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d240b2-f0ec-5826-be4a-8f21e8f0a799" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510043} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c12bf5a-62dd-517a-86dc-485e43650a01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c07b8d08-df25-5edc-8755-7d7271698aeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-157078" :question/problem "Given the QR decomposition $A=QR,$ find the least-squares solution to $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nQ=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5} & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} & -5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,R=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The least-squares solution of $Ax=b$ satisfies the corresponding normal equation:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}Ax={A}^{T}b\n$$\n\nSubstituting $A=QR,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}Ax & ={A}^{T}b \\\\ (QR)^{T}QRx & =(QR)^{T}b \\\\ {R}^{T}({Q}^{T}Q)Rx & ={R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $Q$ has orthonormal columns, ${Q}^{T}Q=I,$ and we get\n\n$$\n{R}^{T}Rx={R}^{T}\\,{Q}^{T}b.\n$$\n\nFinally, since ${R}^{T}$ is invertible, pre-multiplying by $({R}^{T})^{-1}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}Rx & =({R}^{T})^{-1}\\cdot {R}^{T}{Q}^{T}b \\\\ Rx & ={Q}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting our matrices, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}x & =\\overset{{Q}^{T}}{\\overset{⏞}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{70}}[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 3\\sqrt{2} & -5\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]x & =[\\begin{aligned}-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ -10\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{x}_{1}+2\\sqrt{5}{x}_{2}=-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2}{x}_{2}=-10\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-10.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}{x}_{1}+2\\sqrt{5}(-10) & =-10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}{x}_{1} & =10\\sqrt{5} \\\\ {x}_{1} & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the least-squares solution to $Ax=b$ is $[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
